   "text": "This is ruxolitinib-d8: the (R)-3-(cyclopentyl)-3-(pyrazol-1-yl)propanenitrile core carrying the pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine, with eight deuteriums on the cyclopentyl ring.\n\n- **Heteroaromatic part:** a 7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (pyrimidine fused to a pyrrole with an NH) is attached at its C4 position to C4 of a pyrazole ring.\n- **Linker:** the pyrazole N1 is bonded to a stereocentre. That carbon also bears a CH2\u2013C\u2261N arm, drawn on a wedge, and the cyclopentyl ring.\n- **Cyclopentyl ring:** eight \u00b2H labels are shown, two on each of the four CH2 carbons. The ring carbon attached to the stereocentre keeps its ordinary H.\n- **Stereochemistry:** the priorities at the stereocentre are N (pyrazole) > cyclopentyl C > CH2CN > H. With the CH2CN on a wedge and H pointing back, N \u2192 cyclopentyl \u2192 CH2 runs clockwise, so the centre is R. I took the known R-ruxolitinib SMILES `N#CC[C@@H](C1CCCC1)n1cc(cn1)-c1ncnc2[nH]ccc12` as a reference. In my SMILES the pyrazole N and the cyclopentyl C come in the opposite order, so the chirality tag flips to `@`.\n\nSMILES: N#CC[C@H](n1cc(cn1)-c1ncnc2[nH]ccc12)C1C([2H])([2H])C([2H])([2H])C([2H])([2H])C1([2H])[2H]"
